.TH "PW-LOUDCOMP" "1" "2026-08-22"
.SH NAME
.PD
.PP
\fBpw-loudcomp\fP \- Loudness compensation for PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PD
.PP
\fBpw-loudcomp\fP \fIcommand\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PD
.PP
\fBpw-loudcomp\fP is a simple Bash script that automates setting up, connecting, and adjusting the volume of LSP Loudness Compensation\&.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart-daemon\fP
Starts the daemon if it is not running; it is recommended to use the systemd service instead\&.

.TP
\fBstop-daemon\fP
Stops the daemon if it is running; it is recommended to use the systemd service instead\&.

.TP
\fBstart-socket\fP
Starts the socket if it is not running; it is recommended to use the systemd socket instead\&.

.TP
\fBstop-socket\fP
Stops the socket if it is running; it is recommended to use the systemd socket instead\&.

.TP
\fBreload\fP
Manually reloads the configuration instead of restarting the daemon\&.

.TP
\fBcreate-config\fP
Manually creates a configuration file\&.

.TP
\fBset-input-gain\fP \fIvalue\fP
Sets an input gain value or increases or decreases it\&.

.TP
\fBset-volume\fP \fIvalue\fP
Sets a volume value or increases or decreases it\&.

.TP
\fBset-mute-state\fP \fIstate\fP
Specifies whether to mute or unmute the output device\&.

.TP
\fBset-curve-state\fP \fIstate\fP
Specifies whether to enable or disable the correction curve\&.

.TP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP
Displays the help message\&.

.TP
\fBset\fP \fIproperty\fP \fIraw_value\fP
Directly sets values for any LSP loudness compensation symbol parameter\&.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fB2(+/-)\fP
Sets an exact value for \fBset-volume\fP and \fBset-input-gain\fP\&.

.TP
\fB2%(+/-)\fP
Increases or decreases the value relatively for \fBset-volume\fP and \fBset-input-gain\fP\&.

.TP
\fB1/0/toggle\fP
Sets a state for \fBset-mute-state\fP and \fBset-curve-state\fP\&.

.SH SEE ALSO
.PD
.PP
pw\-loudcomp(5)
